Hi James,

I spoke to an Affymetrix application specialist and both of your proposed
possibilities are the case for different tiling array platforms. For some
arrays (such as the yeast tiling array), the .bpmap files are indeed
erroneous and they are currently working on new versions of these files.
For other array platforms (the drosophila tiling array was mentioned)
identical sequences in the genome are only represented once on the array to
save place and thus duplicated entries in the .bpmap file are not
erroneous. Maybe something to take into account for future versions of
pdInfoBuilder as you already mentioned.

Regards,

Ludo.

