The arrayMagic package last appeared in the Bioconductor 2.1 release and 
can still be downloaded for use with R 2.6. Bioconductor employs a 
creative destructive process where software is retired (made defunct) at 
the end of its software life cycle and that happened with arrayMagic 
during the creation of Bioconductor 2.2. When a package is made defunct 
there typically is an alternative package out there that addresses the 
issues handled by the old one. Are there particular applications that 
you were looking to use arrayMagic for?


Patrick


